+## Combining queries
+
+Branches are combined by position, not by name: the result takes its column
+names from the leftmost branch and its column types from the type lattice, so a
+branch on the narrow side of a promotion has its values widened before the two
+are compared.
+
+```console
+$ tanager "CREATE TABLE q1 (city TEXT, sales INTEGER);
+           CREATE TABLE q2 (city TEXT, sales INTEGER);
+           INSERT INTO q1 VALUES ('lisbon', 3), ('oslo', 1), ('lisbon', 3);
+           INSERT INTO q2 VALUES ('lisbon', 3), ('cork', 5);
+           SELECT city FROM q1 EXCEPT SELECT city FROM q2"
+city
+------
+oslo
+(1 rows)
+```
+
 ## Supported SQL grammar (informal)
 
 ```
-statement   := select | insert | create_table | drop_table
+statement   := query | insert | create_table | drop_table
+query       := select { set_op select }
+               [ORDER BY sort_key {, sort_key}] [LIMIT n] [OFFSET n]
+set_op      := (UNION | INTERSECT | EXCEPT) [ALL]
 select      := SELECT [DISTINCT] select_list
                [FROM table [alias] { join }]
                [WHERE expr]
